IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cards-domain`
IMPORT `earn-kernel`
IMPORT `sc-exclusions`
IMPORT fixtures

§ `Standard Chartered Smart Credit Card Promotion — the Smart Rewards Promotion`

-- ===========================================================================
-- DOCUMENT. sc-smart-promo-tnc: "Standard Chartered Smart Credit Card
-- Promotion Terms and Conditions" (Smart Rewards Promotion) on sc.com/sg,
-- clauses 1-18 of the current page, held by clause-text digest. The page
-- carries no version or effective date.
--
-- SUPERSEDED, AND STILL SERVED. The Version 1 August 2024 PDF at av.sc.com
-- (held as role `historical`, sc-smart-promo-tnc-2024) describes a different
-- structure: 1.6 points per S$1 on every Qualifying Smart Card Transaction, a
-- further 17.6 points on named merchants, and a monthly cap of 14,400 points on
-- the further points. The current page has NO CAP and three tiers.
--
-- WHAT THE CURRENT PAGE SAYS.
--   cl.1-2 A valid, in-good-standing Smart Card.
--   cl.3   Eligible Retail Transactions earn 360° Rewards Points "(based on
--          transaction posting date)". Principal and supplementary spend are
--          aggregated (cl.4).
--   cl.5   "Bonus Merchant Transactions" are spends at: Smart Dining (Burger
--          King, Domino's Pizza, KFC, McDonald's, Pizza Hut, Starbucks, Subway,
--          The Coffee Bean & Tea Leaf, Toast Box, Ya Kun Kaya Toast); Smart
--          Streaming (Amazon Prime Video, Disney+, HBO GO, iQIYI, Netflix,
--          Spotify, Viu, YouTube); Smart Transport (BUS/MRT via SimplyGo;
--          Electric Vehicle (EV) charging merchants under MCC 5552, footnoted:
--          "Bonus 360° Rewards Points earned from spends charged to EV charging
--          merchants is only applicable from 6 December 2024 to 31 December
--          2025"). "Base 360° Rewards Points are awarded for all other Eligible
--          Retail Transactions."
--   cl.6   "there is no cap to the number of Base and Bonus 360° Rewards Points
--          a Smart Cardholder can earn each month". "Month" is "the period
--          from the statement date of the current calendar month to one day
--          prior to the statement date of the following calendar month".
--   cl.7   The table, by the month's Eligible Retail Transactions:
--            >= S$1,500  bonus merchants 28.8 + base 3.2 = 32.0 points (10%)
--                        other eligible transactions: base 3.2 (1%)
--            >= S$800    bonus merchants 24.0 + base 1.6 = 25.6 points (8%)
--                        other eligible transactions: base 1.6 (0.5%)
--            <  S$800    "From 1 April 2025, Smart Cardholders will earn the
--                        Base Rewards Points of 1.6 points for all Eligible
--                        Retail Transactions (equivalent to 0.5% cashback) if
--                        the minimum spends of S$800 month is not met." (A 4%
--                        tier for bonus merchants ran 6 December 2024 to 31
--                        March 2025 only.)
--   cl.8   Base points credit on the statement date; Bonus points the day after.
--   cl.9   "A minimum block of 3,200 360° Rewards Points is required to redeem
--          for S$10 cashback", so a point is worth S$10/3,200 = S$0.003125.
--   cl.10  The Retail Transaction Exclusions (sc-exclusions.l4).
--
-- THE TIER IS THE MONTH'S, NOT THE PURCHASE'S. The table sets the rate by the
-- month's Eligible Retail Transactions in total, which the cardholder cannot
-- know until the statement closes. For one purchase the module therefore gives
-- a FLOOR from the tier the month has already reached including this purchase
-- (spend only grows, so it can only rise) and a CEILING from the top tier, and
-- names the condition "the month's Eligible Retail Transactions reach S$800 or
-- S$1,500". A purchase at a non-bonus merchant also has a ceiling above its
-- floor: its base rate rises from 1.6 to 3.2 points at S$1,500.
--
-- THE FORK F-sc-ev. The clause text says the EV-charging bonus ended 31
-- December 2025. MileLion's 6 February 2026 review footnotes it "*Until 31
-- December 2026". The module takes the clause text (EV charging is a Bonus
-- Merchant only to 31 December 2025) and gives a purchase posted from 1 January
-- to 31 December 2026 a floor of the non-bonus rate, a ceiling of the bonus
-- rate, and the open-reading condition. ASSUMED, NOT RULED.
--
-- THE FORK F-sc-simplygo is in sc-exclusions.l4: a bus or train fare whose
-- statement line bears the SIMPLYGO description may or may not be excluded.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `cl.7 -- the table`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Smart month's lower threshold in S$` MEANS 800

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Smart month's upper threshold in S$` MEANS 1500

-- 360° Rewards Points per S$1, by the tier the month has reached.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Smart points per S$1 at a bonus merchant in the top tier` MEANS 32

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Smart points per S$1 at a bonus merchant in the middle tier` MEANS 25.6

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Smart points per S$1 at another merchant in the top tier` MEANS 3.2

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Smart points per S$1 in the bottom tier or at another merchant in the middle tier` MEANS 1.6

-- cl.9: 3,200 points redeem S$10.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the S$ value of one Smart point` MEANS 10 DIVIDED BY 3200

GIVEN total IS A NUMBER, isBonusMerchant IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Smart points per S$1 for a month of` total `at a bonus merchant` isBonusMerchant MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF total AT LEAST `the Smart month's upper threshold in S$`
            THEN IF isBonusMerchant
                 THEN `Smart points per S$1 at a bonus merchant in the top tier`
                 ELSE `Smart points per S$1 at another merchant in the top tier`
        IF total AT LEAST `the Smart month's lower threshold in S$`
            THEN IF isBonusMerchant
                 THEN `Smart points per S$1 at a bonus merchant in the middle tier`
                 ELSE `Smart points per S$1 in the bottom tier or at another merchant in the middle tier`
        OTHERWISE `Smart points per S$1 in the bottom tier or at another merchant in the middle tier`


§§ `cl.5 -- the Bonus Merchants`

GIVEN who IS A Merchant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Smart Dining or Streaming list names` who MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `Burger King`                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Domino's Pizza`               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `KFC`                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `McDonald's`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Pizza Hut`                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Starbucks`                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Subway`                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `The Coffee Bean & Tea Leaf`   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Toast Box`                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Ya Kun Kaya Toast`            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Amazon Prime Video`           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Disney+`                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `HBO GO`                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `iQIYI`                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Netflix`                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Spotify`                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Viu`                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `YouTube`                      THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                                FALSE

-- Smart Transport, first limb: "BUS/MRT via SimplyGo".
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is a SimplyGo fare` p MEANS
    p's merchant EQUALS `SimplyGo` AND p's item EQUALS `A SimplyGo bus or train fare`

-- Smart Transport, second limb: EV charging merchants under MCC 5552.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is EV charging` p MEANS
    `the code is among` p (LIST 5552)

-- The footnote: the EV bonus "is only applicable from 6 December 2024 to 31
-- December 2025". Judged on the posting date (cl.3).
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the EV bonus window holds on the posting date of` p MEANS
    p's `date posted` AT LEAST Date 6 12 2024 AND p's `date posted` AT MOST Date 31 12 2025

-- Posted in 2026: the window the clause text closed and one blog extends.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is EV charging posted in the year the blog extends` p MEANS
    `the purchase is EV charging` p
    AND p's `date posted` AT LEAST Date 1 1 2026 AND p's `date posted` AT MOST Date 31 12 2026

-- A Bonus Merchant Transaction on the clause text. (The EV limb is dated.)
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is a Smart Bonus Merchant Transaction` p MEANS
    `the Smart Dining or Streaming list names` (p's merchant)
    OR `the purchase is a SimplyGo fare` p
    OR (`the purchase is EV charging` p AND `the EV bonus window holds on the posting date of` p)


§§ `The answer for one eligible purchase, on the tier the month has reached`

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
      m IS A `Smart month`
      isBonusMerchant IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Smart points on` p `in the month` m `as a bonus merchant` isBonusMerchant MEANS
    (p's `amount in SGD`) TIMES (`Smart points per S$1 for a month of` ((m's `Eligible Retail Transactions`) PLUS (p's `amount in SGD`)) `at a bonus merchant` isBonusMerchant)

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
      isBonusMerchant IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Smart points on` p `if the month reaches the top tier as a bonus merchant` isBonusMerchant MEANS
    (p's `amount in SGD`) TIMES (`Smart points per S$1 for a month of` 1500 `at a bonus merchant` isBonusMerchant)

-- One evaluation: the purchase is eligible (or not), bonus (or not).
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
      m IS A `Smart month`
      isBonusMerchant IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Smart answer when the merchant is settled` p m isBonusMerchant MEANS
    IF `the SC page excludes` p
    THEN `nothing is earned on` `Standard Chartered Smart` `in` `360° Rewards Points` `per` "Smart Rewards Promotion cl.10 and the Retail Transaction Exclusions"
    ELSE `the answer` (`an answer for` `Standard Chartered Smart` `in` `360° Rewards Points` `of` (`the Smart points on` p `in the month` m `as a bonus merchant` isBonusMerchant) `to` (`the Smart points on` p `if the month reaches the top tier as a bonus merchant` isBonusMerchant) `wanting` (`the Smart points on` p `if the month reaches the top tier as a bonus merchant` isBonusMerchant) `at` NOTHING `excluded` FALSE `drawing on` `No pot` `depending on` (`Smart tier conditions for` p m isBonusMerchant) `per` "Smart Rewards Promotion cl.7") `valued in dollars at` `the S$ value of one Smart point`

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
      m IS A `Smart month`
      isBonusMerchant IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF Condition
`Smart tier conditions for` p m isBonusMerchant MEANS
    IF (`the Smart points on` p `in the month` m `as a bonus merchant` isBonusMerchant) EQUALS (`the Smart points on` p `if the month reaches the top tier as a bonus merchant` isBonusMerchant)
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE LIST `Smart: the month's Eligible Retail Transactions reach S$800 or S$1,500`

GIVEN c IS A Card
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Smart earns nothing under the open reading` c MEANS
    `nothing is earned on` c `in` `360° Rewards Points` `per` "Smart Rewards Promotion cl.5 footnote / Retail Transaction Exclusions (open reading)"

-- The Smart card's answer for one purchase in one statement month.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
      m IS A `Smart month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` p m MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `only the SIMPLYGO entry would exclude` p AND `the purchase is a SimplyGo fare` p
            THEN `bracketed from` (`Smart earns nothing under the open reading` `Standard Chartered Smart`) `to` (`Smart answer when the merchant is settled` p m TRUE) `adding` (LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)
        IF `the purchase is EV charging posted in the year the blog extends` p
            THEN `bracketed from` (`Smart answer when the merchant is settled` p m FALSE) `to` (`Smart answer when the merchant is settled` p m TRUE) `adding` (LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)
        OTHERWISE `Smart answer when the merchant is settled` p m (`the purchase is a Smart Bonus Merchant Transaction` p)


§§ `The clock the Smart tier runs on`

-- cl.3 ("based on transaction posting date") and cl.6.
GIVETH A `Period basis`
`the Smart tier's period` MEANS `Statement period`

GIVETH A `Date basis`
`the Smart tier's date basis` MEANS `Posting date`

#ASSERT `the Smart tier's period` EQUALS `Statement period`
#ASSERT `the Smart tier's date basis` EQUALS `Posting date`


§§ `Illustrations -- built from the cl.7 table and its two worked examples`

GIVEN soFar IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Smart month`
`a Smart month of` soFar MEANS
    `Smart month` WITH `Eligible Retail Transactions` IS soFar

`a McDonald's purchase of S$10` MEANS `purchase for` (`purchase at merchant` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5814) `McDonald's`) 10
`a Netflix purchase of S$20` MEANS `purchase for` (`purchase at merchant` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 4899) `Netflix`) 20
`a purchase at an unnamed shop of S$10` MEANS `purchase for` `the base purchase` 10
`a SimplyGo fare of S$2` MEANS `purchase for` (`purchase of item` (`purchase at merchant` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 4111) `SimplyGo`) `A SimplyGo bus or train fare`) 2
`an EV charge of S$30 posted 20 October 2026` MEANS `purchase for` (`purchase posted on` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5552) (Date 20 10 2026)) 30
`an EV charge of S$30 posted 20 December 2025` MEANS `purchase for` (`purchase posted on` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5552) (Date 20 12 2025)) 30

-- cl.7, the worked example: bonus merchants S$600 of S$1,500 -> 600 x 28.8 = 17,280
-- bonus points plus 1,500 x 3.2 = 4,800 base points = 22,080 points = S$69.00
-- cashback. Per S$1 at a bonus merchant in the top tier: 28.8 + 3.2 = 32.
#ASSERT `Smart points per S$1 for a month of` 1500 `at a bonus merchant` TRUE EQUALS 32
#ASSERT 600 TIMES (`Smart points per S$1 for a month of` 1500 `at a bonus merchant` TRUE) PLUS 900 TIMES (`Smart points per S$1 for a month of` 1500 `at a bonus merchant` FALSE) EQUALS 22080
#ASSERT (22080 TIMES `the S$ value of one Smart point`) EQUALS 69
-- cl.7, the second worked example: bonus S$300 of S$800 -> 300 x 25.6 + 500 x 1.6 = 8,480 points = S$26.50.
#ASSERT 300 TIMES (`Smart points per S$1 for a month of` 800 `at a bonus merchant` TRUE) PLUS 500 TIMES (`Smart points per S$1 for a month of` 800 `at a bonus merchant` FALSE) EQUALS 8480
#ASSERT (8480 TIMES `the S$ value of one Smart point`) EQUALS 26.5

-- The tier boundaries: S$799.99 is the bottom tier, S$800 the middle, S$1,500 the top.
#ASSERT `Smart points per S$1 for a month of` 799.99 `at a bonus merchant` TRUE EQUALS 1.6
#ASSERT `Smart points per S$1 for a month of` 800 `at a bonus merchant` TRUE EQUALS 25.6
#ASSERT `Smart points per S$1 for a month of` 1499.99 `at a bonus merchant` TRUE EQUALS 25.6
#ASSERT `Smart points per S$1 for a month of` 800 `at a bonus merchant` FALSE EQUALS 1.6
#ASSERT `Smart points per S$1 for a month of` 1500 `at a bonus merchant` FALSE EQUALS 3.2

-- A McDonald's purchase in a month that has S$900 already: middle tier, 25.6 x 10 = 256 points,
-- with the top tier (320 points) as the ceiling, the condition named.
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a McDonald's purchase of S$10` (`a Smart month of` 900))'s `units certain` EQUALS 256
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a McDonald's purchase of S$10` (`a Smart month of` 900))'s `units at best` EQUALS 320
#ASSERT elem `Smart: the month's Eligible Retail Transactions reach S$800 or S$1,500` ((`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a McDonald's purchase of S$10` (`a Smart month of` 900))'s `depends on`)
-- ... in a month that has S$1,500 already: the top tier, certain = best, no condition.
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a McDonald's purchase of S$10` (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s `units certain` EQUALS 320
#ASSERT null ((`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a McDonald's purchase of S$10` (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s `depends on`)
-- ... in an empty month: the bottom tier, 1.6 x 10 = 16 points, ceiling 320.
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a McDonald's purchase of S$10` (`a Smart month of` 0))'s `units certain` EQUALS 16
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a McDonald's purchase of S$10` (`a Smart month of` 0))'s `units at best` EQUALS 320
-- ... this purchase itself can lift the month over S$800: S$795 so far + S$10 = S$805 -> 25.6 x 10.
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a McDonald's purchase of S$10` (`a Smart month of` 795))'s `units certain` EQUALS 256

-- Streaming is a Bonus Merchant; an unnamed shop is not.
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a Netflix purchase of S$20` (`a Smart month of` 800))'s `units certain` EQUALS 512
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a purchase at an unnamed shop of S$10` (`a Smart month of` 800))'s `units certain` EQUALS 16
-- ... whose ceiling is the top tier's 1% (3.2 per S$1 = 32 points for S$10).
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a purchase at an unnamed shop of S$10` (`a Smart month of` 800))'s `units at best` EQUALS 32

-- Cash value: 3,200 points redeem S$10.
#ASSERT fromMaybe 0 ((`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a McDonald's purchase of S$10` (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s `cash value certain`) EQUALS 1
-- No miles: the points redeem for cashback, and no held document converts them to miles.
#ASSERT isNothing ((`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a McDonald's purchase of S$10` (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s `miles certain`)

-- SimplyGo bus and train fares are Bonus Merchant Transactions.
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `a SimplyGo fare of S$2` (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s `units certain` EQUALS 64
-- ... unless the statement line bears the SIMPLYGO description: the open reading (floor 0).
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` (`purchase described as` `a SimplyGo fare of S$2` `SimplyGo as a descriptor`) (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` (`purchase described as` `a SimplyGo fare of S$2` `SimplyGo as a descriptor`) (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s `units at best` EQUALS 64

-- EV charging: a Bonus Merchant only in the window 6 December 2024 to 31 December 2025.
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `an EV charge of S$30 posted 20 December 2025` (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s `units certain` EQUALS 960
-- ... posted in 2026 the clause text ended it: floor is the base rate (3.2 x 30 = 96), ceiling the bonus, open.
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `an EV charge of S$30 posted 20 October 2026` (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s `units certain` EQUALS 96
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `an EV charge of S$30 posted 20 October 2026` (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s `units at best` EQUALS 960
#ASSERT elem `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)` ((`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` `an EV charge of S$30 posted 20 October 2026` (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s `depends on`)

-- Exclusions apply: a cash advance, a reversed charge, a listed MCC.
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` (`purchase of kind` `a McDonald's purchase of S$10` `Cash advance`) (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` (`purchase later reversed` `a McDonald's purchase of S$10`) (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`Standard Chartered Smart earns on` (`recoded purchase` `a McDonald's purchase of S$10` 7523) (`a Smart month of` 1500))'s excluded
